27
00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:28.370
I really wanted to meet her, so Kelly, are you there?

28
00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:29.467
Yeah!

29
00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:31.653
Hi, Kelly, how are you?

30
00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:34.443
(clearing throat)

31
00:01:34.443 --> 00:01:35.276
Excuse me.

32
00:01:35.276 --> 00:01:36.185
Speaking of pets.

33
00:01:36.185 --> 00:01:37.018
(coughing)

34
00:01:37.018 --> 00:01:38.709
I have a frog in my throat.

35
00:01:38.709 --> 00:01:40.590
Oh my gosh. I do too,

36
00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:42.660
because I'm just so excited to meet you.

37
00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.080
Thank you!

38
00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:47.620
Oh, I'm so glad you're here and when I heard your story,

39
00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.150
I just thought, okay,

40
00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.900
I wanted to tell the story of my morning

41
00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:56.980
because our pets are so important to us

42
00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:01.980
and you started a food pantry for pets out of your garage,

43
00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:06.220
so that people could take care of their animals.

44
00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:09.120
I mean, what gave you the idea to do that?

45
00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.880
Yeah, so I've been a rescuer for a long time,

46
00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:15.380
a solid rescuer since 2012, I love animals

47
00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:18.740
and I know that that's always an issue,

48
00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:22.510 line:15%
needing pet food and needing care and so with the pandemic,

49
00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:24.610 line:15%
I just knew things were that much worse.

50
00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:27.510 line:15%
I was hearing so many stories of individuals

51
00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:29.040
having to surrender their pets

52
00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.380
due to not being able to feed them

53
00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.610
and, you know, that's heart-wrenching.

54
00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:35.440
They're like our children, right?

55
00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:37.250
You know, you just talked about all your babies

56
00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.500
in your bed with you and your kids

57
00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.020
and that's heartbreaking.

58
00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.860
I feel like during such trying times,

59
00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:44.760 line:15%
that's the last thing that a family needs,

60
00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.830 line:15%
is to have to surrender their pet,

61
00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:50.130 line:15%
so I just decided to take to Facebook

62
00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:52.500
and see if there was any way that I could help

63
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.220
local families in need.

64
00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.700
And what responses did you get?

65
00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.670
Oh my gosh, Drew, it was so crazy.

66
00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.870
On both sides of the coin,

67
00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:04.260
there were so many, so many individuals that wanted to help.

68
00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.590
I couldn't believe how many folks were offering

69
00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:09.540
to send and bring food and then on top of that,

70
00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:11.290
I actually set some days where I would actually go out

71
00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.090
into the community and help folks

72
00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:14.700
who didn't have transportation,

73
00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.290
who couldn't come pick up the food and Drew,

74
00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:19.390
that was actually the hardest part for me

75
00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:23.337
because when I put out a post asking, you know,

76
00:03:23.337 --> 00:03:26.470
"Hey, if you aren't able to get to me, but I can deliver,"

77
00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.640
I got some of the saddest stories, you know?

78
00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:29.860
I would end up in places

79
00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:34.670
that you could really tell that the need was, yeah.

80
00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:38.070
I mean, Kelly, we want to continue to help you

81
00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:38.910
spread the love,

82
00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:42.050
so we reached out to our friends at Petco

83
00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:43.790
and I'm such a Petco fan.

84
00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:48.790
So because of you, they wanna give you $5000 for vet bills

85
00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:54.990
and another $5000 for pet food.

86
00:03:56.345 --> 00:03:57.260
Yes!

87
00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:59.210
Thank you, Petco!

88
00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.610
Thank you so much.

89
00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:03.680
I can't even begin to tell you, the vet bills too!

90
00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.000
That's something else we've been trying so hard to work on.

91
00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:06.993
That is so huge!

92
00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:11.290
Well, you inspired us to think differently

93
00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.630
and the fact that you are thinking differently

94
00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:15.630
is just such a great benefit

95
00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:18.890
to creatures on four and two legs

96
00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:20.909
and so thank you for all that you are doing.

97
00:04:20.909 --> 00:04:23.462
Thank you, I did not expect that!

98
00:04:23.462 --> 00:04:25.516
That is so awesome!

99
00:04:25.516 --> 00:04:26.349
Thank you.

100
00:04:26.349 --> 00:04:27.930
I can't wait to see you do more

101
00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:31.150
and we'll keep in touch and see how it's all going.

102
00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:32.773
Thank you.
Thank you.

103
00:04:33.825 --> 00:04:36.599
Yay, yay!

104
00:04:36.599 --> 00:04:39.266 line:15%
(upbeat music)

